title: Proposition 12
---
order: 12
---
short_label: IX.12
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: If as many numbers as we please beginning from a unit are in continued proportion, then by whatever prime numbers the last is measured, the next to the unit is also measured by the same.
----
proof:

Let {A}, {B}, {C}, and {D} be as many numbers as we please beginning from a unit in continued proportion.

I say that, by whatever prime numbers {D} is measured, {A} is also measured by the same.

Let {D} be measured by any prime number {E}.

I say that {E} measures {A}.

Suppose it does not.

